# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "April 2026 {#april-2026}"
msgstr "April 2026 {#april-2026}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"executor-primitive\"></span>\n"
"- **Introducing the Executor primitive**: We're excited to announce the release of the new `Executor` primitive and a new version of the noise-learning helper class, `NoiseLearnerV3`, both of which were first previewed at QDC 2025.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Together with [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html), they make up the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), which provides full transparency and control to fine-tune your error mitigation workflow. The [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) tutorial, for example, demonstrates how this model is used to combine advanced techniques, including shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), and [measurement-based postselection](/guides/post-selection), to further improve the result quality.\n"
msgstr "  Bersama dengan [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html), keduanya membentuk [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), yang memberikan transparansi dan kontrol penuh untuk menyempurnakan alur kerja mitigasi error kamu. Tutorial [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html), misalnya, menunjukkan bagaimana model ini digunakan untuk menggabungkan teknik-teknik lanjutan, termasuk shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), dan [postselection berbasis pengukuran](/guides/post-selection), untuk lebih meningkatkan kualitas hasil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If you prefer a higher level of abstraction, [`EstimatorV2`](/guides/estimator-noise-management) in Qiskit Runtime continues to provide several built-in error mitigation and suppression techniques, which you can easily tune using the [`resilience_level`](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience-level) option.\n"
msgstr "  Jika kamu lebih menyukai tingkat abstraksi yang lebih tinggi, [`EstimatorV2`](/guides/estimator-noise-management) di Qiskit Runtime tetap menyediakan beberapa teknik mitigasi dan supresi error bawaan, yang bisa kamu sesuaikan dengan mudah menggunakan opsi [`resilience_level`](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience-level).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  To learn more, see the following guides:\n"
msgstr "  Untuk mempelajari lebih lanjut, lihat panduan berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Executor quickstart](/guides/get-started-with-executor)\n"
msgstr "[Panduan cepat Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning)\n"
msgstr "[Pembantu noise learning](/guides/noise-learning)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Both of these new features are currently in beta and require `qiskit-ibm-runtime` version 0.47.0 or higher.\n"
msgstr "  Kedua fitur baru ini saat ini dalam versi beta dan membutuhkan `qiskit-ibm-runtime` versi 0.47.0 atau lebih tinggi.\n"

